[quote="Silverleaf"]

I&#39;m genuinely curious, what&#39;s the advantage?

[/quote]

It&#39;s just to keep track over everything on the table so you don&#39;t miss anything.

We&#39;re pretty casual players, so it&#39;s kind of a bummer when we realize we haven&#39;t been doing X dmg from some minion because we forgot after reading it or something.

Really we didn&#39;t even consider anything like this until everyone was reading over the setup for Vengence, and everyone went &quot;well... I don&#39;t really wana keep track of 11 decks with all their cards out, lets just play vs a single boss&quot;

&nbsp;

The idea was basically just a helper app, keeps everythign straight for you. But if you don&#39;t have something as simple as scanning a QR code, then you would have to have an interface where you tell it which card was played.. which would just be a solid &quot;no, never, ever&quot;

The game is fun because it&#39;s a card game,&nbsp;I dunno how fun it would be as a purely digital game, so the idea isn&#39;t to turn it in to that; it&#39;s just to leverage a smart-devices to make sure you keep track of everything.

&nbsp;

I do want to say I&#39;m a pretty big fan of SofM, you guys have done a great job. It&#39;s hard to find a game to play (board&nbsp;or card)&nbsp;that has a level of sophistication that is engaging, but not so much so that no one wants to learn how to do it.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

